  "interpretation": [
    "This reports only isolated note_midi-labeled windows from two GuitarSet solo tracks per player. Selection and label quality are not independently adjudicated.",
    "Players 00/01 were development; players 02/03 were held out. No training occurred and thresholds were not adjusted after development or holdout.",
    "A match is a stable, prior-free YIN note/octave observation. The UI does not use this gate yet. Different-note false calls were zero among 47 accepted holdout windows, but this small sample does not establish real-device reliability.",
    "Development player 00 had 7/22 coverage because the track-derived room-floor estimate rejected quiet segments; the app must calibrate the actual room before any live use.",
    "Studio mono-mic takes do not represent built-in iOS/Android microphones, room noise, accompaniment, wrong-note attempts, chords or users with varied instruments. The founder authorized future opt-in on-device single-note tracking without raw audio storage or upload; native capture was absent at this initial offline replay stage. Subsequent opt-in observation wiring and separate players 04/05 replay are documented in guitar-note-observation-2026-09-26.json; physical-phone acceptance and user-facing scoring gates remain open.",
    "dB in this evaluation is digital dBFS relative to an estimated recording floor, not acoustic dB(A) or hearing exposure."
  ]
